1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,111
Have you ever looked at someone and wondered how Allah has

2
00:00:03,111 --> 00:00:04,932
blessed them with so much?

3
00:00:05,016 --> 00:00:08,742
They have a successful business, a beautiful family,

4
00:00:08,742 --> 00:00:14,998
financial stability, and opportunities that seem to come one after another.

5
00:00:15,139 --> 00:00:18,065
Meanwhile, you might be working hard,

6
00:00:18,065 --> 00:00:22,581
making dua, trying your best, but still struggling to make ends

7
00:00:22,581 --> 00:00:23,220
meet.

8
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:25,727
You might even find yourself asking:

9
00:00:25,727 --> 00:00:29,059
"Why does my rizq feel so limited?"

10
00:00:29,059 --> 00:00:32,391
But what if I told you that Islam teaches us about

11
00:00:32,391 --> 00:00:36,511
ways to seek greater provision and blessings from Allah?

12
00:00:36,652 --> 00:00:38,879
And here is something important.

13
00:00:38,904 --> 00:00:40,983
Rizq is not just money.

14
00:00:40,983 --> 00:00:42,341
It is your health.

15
00:00:42,341 --> 00:00:43,490
Your family.

16
00:00:43,490 --> 00:00:44,860
Your peace of mind.

17
00:00:44,860 --> 00:00:45,928
Your time.

18
00:00:45,928 --> 00:00:47,461
Your opportunities.

19
00:00:47,461 --> 00:00:51,303
And even the ability to wake up every morning with faith

20
00:00:51,303 --> 00:00:52,497
in your heart.

21
00:00:52,580 --> 00:00:56,876
The Quran and Sunnah teach us several powerful ways to seek

22
00:00:56,876 --> 00:00:58,476
Allah's blessings.

23
00:00:58,502 --> 00:01:01,367
Today, we're going through eight of them.

24
00:01:01,392 --> 00:01:04,943
Before we begin, we need to understand something.

25
00:01:05,026 --> 00:01:08,067
Allah is Ar-Razzaq, the Provider.

26
00:01:08,092 --> 00:01:10,437
Every provision comes from Him.

27
00:01:10,437 --> 00:01:16,973
In Surah Adh-Dhariyat, verse 58, Allah describes Himself as the Provider,

28
00:01:16,973 --> 00:01:19,781
the Possessor of power and strength.

29
00:01:19,864 --> 00:01:21,151
Think about that.

30
00:01:21,176 --> 00:01:24,485
Every meal you eat, every breath you take,

31
00:01:24,485 --> 00:01:28,350
and every blessing you enjoy comes from Allah.

32
00:01:28,653 --> 00:01:32,694
But sometimes we become so focused on what we don't have

33
00:01:32,694 --> 00:01:36,883
that we forget everything Allah has already given us.

34
00:01:37,187 --> 00:01:40,110
We compare our lives to other people.

35
00:01:40,252 --> 00:01:42,736
We see someone buying a new car,

36
00:01:42,736 --> 00:01:45,592
purchasing a house, or becoming wealthy,

37
00:01:45,592 --> 00:01:48,191
and suddenly we feel behind.

38
00:01:48,332 --> 00:01:52,419
But someone's financial situation does not determine their worth in the

39
00:01:52,419 --> 00:01:53,835
eyes of Allah.

40
00:01:53,835 --> 00:01:57,957
And having more money does not automatically mean Allah is more

41
00:01:57,957 --> 00:01:59,940
pleased with that person.

42
00:02:00,151 --> 00:02:03,425
Your goal should not simply be to become wealthy.

43
00:02:03,425 --> 00:02:06,548
Your goal should be to seek halal provision,

44
00:02:06,548 --> 00:02:11,167
beneficial blessings, and a life that brings you closer to Allah.

45
00:02:11,308 --> 00:02:14,661
So let's look at eight ways to seek that rizq.

46
00:02:14,802 --> 00:02:18,297
The first way is to increase your istighfar.

47
00:02:18,297 --> 00:02:22,035
Istighfar means asking Allah for forgiveness.

48
00:02:22,035 --> 00:02:26,132
And this is directly connected to provision in the Quran.

49
00:02:26,273 --> 00:02:29,106
In Surah Nuh, verses 10 to 12,

50
00:02:29,106 --> 00:02:31,532
Prophet Nuh, peace be upon him,

51
00:02:31,532 --> 00:02:35,050
tells his people to seek forgiveness from their Lord.

52
00:02:35,050 --> 00:02:40,019
He explains that Allah will send abundant rain and increase them

53
00:02:40,019 --> 00:02:44,475
in wealth and children, and provide gardens and rivers.

54
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:46,426
Think about the connection.

55
00:02:46,509 --> 00:02:50,967
Seeking forgiveness is not only about asking Allah to forgive your

56
00:02:50,967 --> 00:02:52,579
past mistakes.

57
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:55,936
It is also an act of worship through which you seek

58
00:02:55,936 --> 00:02:58,315
His mercy and blessings.

59
00:02:58,398 --> 00:03:02,926
Sometimes we spend hours worrying about money but very little time

60
00:03:02,926 --> 00:03:05,246
asking Allah for forgiveness.

61
00:03:05,387 --> 00:03:08,856
Make istighfar part of your daily routine.

62
00:03:08,905 --> 00:03:09,648
Say:

63
00:03:09,648 --> 00:03:11,283
Astaghfirullah.

64
00:03:11,285 --> 00:03:12,817
Astaghfirullah.

65
00:03:12,817 --> 00:03:14,522
Astaghfirullah.

66
00:03:14,779 --> 00:03:18,251
Say it sincerely, understand what you're asking for,

67
00:03:18,251 --> 00:03:21,200
and try to leave the sins you are asking Allah to

68
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:22,196
forgive.

69
00:03:22,198 --> 00:03:25,600
You don't need to wait until your life becomes difficult to

70
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:27,328
turn back to Allah.

71
00:03:27,411 --> 00:03:30,103
The second way is to develop taqwa.

72
00:03:30,128 --> 00:03:34,782
Taqwa means being conscious of Allah and trying to obey Him.

73
00:03:34,923 --> 00:03:37,837
In Surah At-Talaq, verses 2 and 3,

74
00:03:37,837 --> 00:03:41,053
Allah tells us that whoever has taqwa of Him,

75
00:03:41,053 --> 00:03:43,816
He will make a way out for them and provide for

76
00:03:43,816 --> 00:03:46,823
them from places they could never imagine.

77
00:03:46,823 --> 00:03:48,505
Let that sink in.

78
00:03:48,715 --> 00:03:53,046
Allah promises a way out and provision from unexpected sources for

79
00:03:53,046 --> 00:03:54,683
those who have taqwa.

80
00:03:54,683 --> 00:03:59,546
This doesn't mean a believer will never experience financial difficulties.

81
00:03:59,629 --> 00:04:02,530
Even the prophets experienced hardship.

82
00:04:02,613 --> 00:04:05,991
But it reminds us that our provision is not limited to

83
00:04:05,991 --> 00:04:08,799
the opportunities we can currently see.

84
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:10,821
So protect your prayers.

85
00:04:10,821 --> 00:04:13,457
Stay away from what Allah has forbidden.

86
00:04:13,457 --> 00:04:15,500
Be honest in your business.

87
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:18,403
And remember Allah when making decisions.

88
00:04:18,403 --> 00:04:22,998
Never sacrifice your relationship with Allah just to chase more money.

89
00:04:23,081 --> 00:04:25,833
The third way is tawakkul.

90
00:04:25,833 --> 00:04:29,280
Tawakkul means placing your trust in Allah.

91
00:04:29,305 --> 00:04:32,428
But here's something many people misunderstand.

92
00:04:32,428 --> 00:04:36,247
Trusting Allah does not mean sitting at home doing nothing and

93
00:04:36,247 --> 00:04:38,428
expecting money to appear.

94
00:04:38,453 --> 00:04:40,485
You still have to make an effort.

95
00:04:40,485 --> 00:04:41,832
You look for work.

96
00:04:41,832 --> 00:04:43,631
You learn new skills.

97
00:04:43,631 --> 00:04:45,326
You build your business.

98
00:04:45,326 --> 00:04:47,068
You take responsibility.

99
00:04:47,068 --> 00:04:51,176
But you understand that the final outcome belongs to Allah.

100
00:04:51,317 --> 00:04:54,568
The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him,

101
00:04:54,568 --> 00:04:57,714
taught that if people truly relied upon Allah,

102
00:04:57,714 --> 00:05:00,872
He would provide for them just as He provides for the

103
00:05:00,872 --> 00:05:01,880
birds.

104
00:05:02,021 --> 00:05:05,608
The birds leave their nests hungry in the morning and return

105
00:05:05,608 --> 00:05:07,348
full in the evening.

106
00:05:07,373 --> 00:05:09,289
Notice something important.

107
00:05:09,289 --> 00:05:11,493
They still leave their nests.

108
00:05:11,518 --> 00:05:13,039
They still search.

109
00:05:13,039 --> 00:05:14,804
They still make an effort.

110
00:05:14,804 --> 00:05:16,975
And Allah provides for them.

111
00:05:16,975 --> 00:05:21,235
So work hard, make dua, take the necessary steps,

112
00:05:21,235 --> 00:05:23,799
and trust Allah with the results.

113
00:05:23,824 --> 00:05:27,238
Do not let fear of poverty destroy your trust in your

114
00:05:27,238 --> 00:05:28,327
Creator.

115
00:05:28,410 --> 00:05:32,066
The fourth way is maintaining family relationships.

116
00:05:32,091 --> 00:05:36,630
In today's world, people sometimes become so focused on making money

117
00:05:36,630 --> 00:05:39,440
that they forget about their own families.

118
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:41,646
They stop calling their parents.

119
00:05:41,646 --> 00:05:43,619
They avoid their siblings.

120
00:05:43,619 --> 00:05:47,936
They allow small arguments to turn into years of silence.

121
00:05:47,962 --> 00:05:52,455
But Islam places enormous importance on family ties.

122
00:05:52,455 --> 00:05:57,795
In Sahih al-Bukhari, the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him,

123
00:05:57,795 --> 00:06:01,847
taught that whoever wishes for their provision to be expanded and

124
00:06:01,847 --> 00:06:06,479
their life to be prolonged should maintain their ties of kinship.

125
00:06:06,479 --> 00:06:08,987
Think about how powerful that is.

126
00:06:08,987 --> 00:06:11,611
Something as simple as checking on your mother,

127
00:06:11,611 --> 00:06:14,560
calling your father, visiting a relative,

128
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:18,447
or helping a family member can become an act of worship.

129
00:06:18,472 --> 00:06:22,303
Don't allow money and worldly success to make you forget the

130
00:06:22,303 --> 00:06:25,043
people who were there before you had anything.

131
00:06:25,043 --> 00:06:31,452
Keep your family connections alive, while maintaining appropriate boundaries where necessary.

132
00:06:31,452 --> 00:06:34,052
The fifth way is giving charity.

133
00:06:34,052 --> 00:06:37,721
Some people become afraid of giving money because they think they

134
00:06:37,721 --> 00:06:39,019
will have less.

135
00:06:39,103 --> 00:06:41,332
They look at their bank account and think:

136
00:06:41,332 --> 00:06:43,654
"If I give some of this away,

137
00:06:43,654 --> 00:06:45,788
what if I need it later?"

138
00:06:45,813 --> 00:06:49,192
But the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him,

139
00:06:49,192 --> 00:06:51,605
taught us something beautiful.

140
00:06:51,909 --> 00:06:56,204
In Sahih Muslim, he said that charity does not decrease wealth.

141
00:06:56,204 --> 00:06:59,478
This is not a promise that every donation will return as

142
00:06:59,478 --> 00:07:01,508
a larger amount of cash.

143
00:07:01,649 --> 00:07:04,517
It teaches us that charity brings reward,

144
00:07:04,517 --> 00:07:08,256
blessing, and goodness that cannot simply be measured by a bank

145
00:07:08,256 --> 00:07:09,229
balance.

146
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:12,282
You don't need to be rich to give charity.

147
00:07:12,366 --> 00:07:14,142
You can give a small amount.

148
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:15,895
You can feed someone.

149
00:07:15,895 --> 00:07:18,380
You can help a person who is struggling.

150
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:20,712
You can support a good cause.

151
00:07:21,016 --> 00:07:24,264
And even a kind word can be an act of charity.

152
00:07:24,290 --> 00:07:26,960
Give sincerely for the sake of Allah.

153
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:30,615
Don't give just because you expect something back.

154
00:07:30,698 --> 00:07:33,763
Give because you believe in the mercy and reward of your

155
00:07:33,763 --> 00:07:34,483
Lord.

156
00:07:34,483 --> 00:07:37,059
The sixth way is gratitude.

157
00:07:37,363 --> 00:07:41,728
Sometimes we spend so much time asking Allah for more that

158
00:07:41,728 --> 00:07:45,058
we forget to thank Him for what we already have.

159
00:07:45,455 --> 00:07:48,891
You might be asking for a bigger house while someone else

160
00:07:48,891 --> 00:07:52,245
is asking Allah for a safe place to sleep.

161
00:07:52,549 --> 00:07:55,893
You might be complaining about your job while someone else is

162
00:07:55,893 --> 00:07:58,399
desperately searching for employment.

163
00:07:58,540 --> 00:08:02,197
You might be frustrated with your daily routine while someone else

164
00:08:02,197 --> 00:08:05,945
wishes they could experience another ordinary day.

165
00:08:06,342 --> 00:08:09,476
In Surah Ibrahim, verse 7, Allah says:

166
00:08:09,476 --> 00:08:12,888
"If you are grateful, I will surely increase you."

167
00:08:13,029 --> 00:08:16,487
This is one of the most powerful reminders in the Quran.

168
00:08:16,512 --> 00:08:19,484
Gratitude changes the way you look at life.

169
00:08:19,484 --> 00:08:22,642
Instead of constantly focusing on what is missing,

170
00:08:22,642 --> 00:08:26,346
you begin recognizing the blessings already surrounding you.

171
00:08:26,346 --> 00:08:28,319
Thank Allah for your health.

172
00:08:28,319 --> 00:08:30,409
Thank Allah for your family.

173
00:08:30,409 --> 00:08:32,394
Thank Allah for your food.

174
00:08:32,394 --> 00:08:34,937
Thank Allah for your ability to pray.

175
00:08:34,937 --> 00:08:38,302
And thank Allah even during difficult moments.

176
00:08:38,327 --> 00:08:42,158
Being grateful does not mean pretending that life is perfect.

177
00:08:42,158 --> 00:08:45,374
It means recognizing that even during hardship,

178
00:08:45,374 --> 00:08:48,797
Allah has given you blessings worth appreciating.

179
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:53,350
The seventh way is making sure your income is halal.

180
00:08:53,350 --> 00:08:55,834
This is extremely important.

181
00:08:55,834 --> 00:08:59,689
Some people become so desperate to become wealthy that they are

182
00:08:59,689 --> 00:09:01,128
willing to do anything.

183
00:09:01,128 --> 00:09:02,835
They lie to customers.

184
00:09:02,835 --> 00:09:04,635
They cheat in business.

185
00:09:04,635 --> 00:09:06,573
They take advantage of people.

186
00:09:06,573 --> 00:09:09,392
They earn money through forbidden means.

187
00:09:09,475 --> 00:09:12,691
But what is the value of wealth if it takes you

188
00:09:12,691 --> 00:09:14,756
further away from Allah?

189
00:09:14,886 --> 00:09:20,447
In Surah Al-Baqarah, verse 168, Allah tells humanity to eat from

190
00:09:20,447 --> 00:09:23,732
what is lawful and good on earth and not follow the

191
00:09:23,732 --> 00:09:25,565
footsteps of Shaytan.

192
00:09:25,683 --> 00:09:27,806
Your income matters.

193
00:09:27,935 --> 00:09:30,164
How you make your money matters.

194
00:09:30,164 --> 00:09:32,496
And how you spend it matters.

195
00:09:32,695 --> 00:09:35,178
If you run a business, be honest.

196
00:09:35,261 --> 00:09:39,429
If you work for someone, fulfill your responsibilities.

197
00:09:39,429 --> 00:09:43,560
If you sell something, don't deceive your customers.

198
00:09:43,690 --> 00:09:47,080
Do not chase a bigger bank balance at the expense of

199
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:48,343
your akhirah.

200
00:09:48,368 --> 00:09:52,780
A smaller halal income with blessings is better than wealth obtained

201
00:09:52,780 --> 00:09:55,114
through disobedience to Allah.

202
00:09:55,114 --> 00:09:57,738
The eighth way is making dua.

203
00:09:57,738 --> 00:10:01,242
Never underestimate the power of asking Allah.

204
00:10:01,325 --> 00:10:04,472
Sometimes we ask everyone around us for help,

205
00:10:04,472 --> 00:10:07,872
but forget to ask the One who controls everything.

206
00:10:08,268 --> 00:10:10,451
Allah tells us in Surah Al-Baqarah,

207
00:10:10,451 --> 00:10:14,630
verse 186, that He is near and responds to the call

208
00:10:14,630 --> 00:10:16,708
of the one who calls upon Him.

209
00:10:16,708 --> 00:10:19,075
So ask Allah for provision.

210
00:10:19,158 --> 00:10:21,571
Ask Him for a halal job.

211
00:10:21,654 --> 00:10:23,916
Ask Him to bless your business.

212
00:10:23,941 --> 00:10:27,306
Ask Him to remove your financial difficulties.

213
00:10:27,331 --> 00:10:29,872
Ask Him to protect you from debt.

214
00:10:30,013 --> 00:10:33,125
Ask Him to give you wealth that brings you closer to

215
00:10:33,125 --> 00:10:36,188
Him instead of distracting you from Him.

216
00:10:36,329 --> 00:10:38,640
And don't only ask for money.

217
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:40,333
Ask for barakah.

218
00:10:40,729 --> 00:10:43,481
Because a person can have a large amount of money and

219
00:10:43,481 --> 00:10:45,906
still feel like they have nothing.

220
00:10:46,209 --> 00:10:49,681
But another person can have less and feel content,

221
00:10:49,681 --> 00:10:51,502
peaceful, and grateful.

222
00:10:51,712 --> 00:10:55,312
That is why we should ask Allah not just for more,

223
00:10:55,312 --> 00:10:57,912
but for what is good for us in this life and

224
00:10:57,912 --> 00:10:58,967
the next.

225
00:10:59,271 --> 00:11:02,833
So let's go through the eight ways one more time.

226
00:11:02,916 --> 00:11:05,016
Increase your istighfar.

227
00:11:05,099 --> 00:11:06,780
Develop taqwa.

228
00:11:06,863 --> 00:11:10,114
Put your trust in Allah while making an effort.

229
00:11:10,114 --> 00:11:12,552
Maintain your family relationships.

230
00:11:12,552 --> 00:11:13,655
Give charity.

231
00:11:13,655 --> 00:11:14,874
Be grateful.

232
00:11:14,874 --> 00:11:16,824
Earn through halal means.

233
00:11:16,824 --> 00:11:19,042
And never stop making dua.

234
00:11:19,042 --> 00:11:20,540
But remember something.

235
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:25,484
These are not eight magic steps that guarantee instant wealth.

236
00:11:25,509 --> 00:11:28,330
Rizq is ultimately in the hands of Allah.

237
00:11:28,330 --> 00:11:30,396
Sometimes He gives you wealth.

238
00:11:30,396 --> 00:11:32,753
Sometimes He gives you patience.

239
00:11:32,753 --> 00:11:37,303
Sometimes He protects you from something you never knew was harmful.

240
00:11:37,328 --> 00:11:41,159
And sometimes what you consider a delay is part of a

241
00:11:41,159 --> 00:11:43,794
wisdom you cannot yet understand.

242
00:11:43,794 --> 00:11:47,405
So stop comparing your rizq to everyone else's.

243
00:11:47,405 --> 00:11:48,554
Work hard.

244
00:11:48,554 --> 00:11:50,075
Pray your Salah.

245
00:11:50,075 --> 00:11:51,526
Seek forgiveness.

246
00:11:51,526 --> 00:11:55,485
And trust the One who has provided for you every single

247
00:11:55,485 --> 00:11:57,283
day of your life.

248
00:11:57,424 --> 00:11:59,827
May Allah grant us halal rizq,

249
00:11:59,827 --> 00:12:04,704
abundant barakah, freedom from debt, contentment in our hearts,

250
00:12:04,704 --> 00:12:07,525
and wealth that brings us closer to Him.

251
00:12:07,525 --> 00:12:08,488
Ameen.

252
00:12:08,488 --> 00:12:10,218
And Allah knows best.
